        "id": 27155547,
        "name": null,
        "username": "Gabbatha-grobbulus",
        "avatar_template": "https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/classic-us/character/grobbulus/50/66421810-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/2-1.jpg",
        "created_at": "2025-06-28T11:25:47.081Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This was something we asked ChatGPT: “<em>How can I surpass the Jackal of Stormwind’s Honorable Kill record in enemy capital cities on World of Warcraft, which stands at 10,000?</em>”</p>\n<p>Ah, you’re aiming to <em>surpass</em> the legendary Jackal of Stormwind and set a new standard for the ultimate ganker in WoW? That’s a goal worthy of a true Azerothian legend. Hitting 10,000 Honorable Kills (HKs) in enemy capitals is no small feat — it’s an achievement only the most dedicated, ruthless, and strategic players can pull off.</p>\n<p>But don’t worry, I’ve got your back with some tips on how to dethrone Jackal and make a name for yourself as the true king (or queen) of capital city mayhem. It’s not just about raw numbers, but about <em>strategy</em>, patience, and the right mindset.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-step-by-step-guide-to-surpassing-jackals-record-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-step-by-step-guide-to-surpassing-jackals-record-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>Step-by-Step Guide to Surpassing Jackal’s Record:</strong></h3>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-1-pick-your-ideal-class-for-ganking-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-1-pick-your-ideal-class-for-ganking-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>1. <strong>Pick Your Ideal Class for Ganking</strong></h3>\n<p>To rack up a ton of kills in enemy capitals, you need the right class that thrives in chaotic, PvP-heavy zones.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rogue</strong> – Stealth and burst damage are your bread and butter. You can pick off unsuspecting targets and vanish before reinforcements arrive.</li>\n<li><strong>Druid (Feral or Balance)</strong> – Stealth, mobility, and great burst. Cat form for quick ganks, or Moonkin for mass AoE chaos.</li>\n<li><strong>Hunter</strong> – Pets are a bonus, and your mobility, range, and crowd control are huge for disrupting enemies.</li>\n<li><strong>Warlock</strong> – Fear, DoTs, and an army of demons. You can put pressure on large groups and cause massive disruption.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-2-prepare-for-long-term-commitment-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-2-prepare-for-long-term-commitment-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>2. <strong>Prepare for Long-Term Commitment</strong></h3>\n<p>Getting 10,000 kills in enemy capitals isn’t something you can do in a single weekend. You’ll need to pace yourself and stay consistent.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Plan for multiple sessions</strong>: A “kill streak” of 10,000 will likely take months, so don’t expect immediate results. This is a marathon, not a sprint.</li>\n<li><strong>Divide your time</strong>: Rather than focusing solely on the capital city (though that will be your main base), mix in some battlegrounds, world PvP, and open-world ganking to keep things fresh.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-3-pick-your-capital-target-wisely-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-3-pick-your-capital-target-wisely-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>3. <strong>Pick Your Capital Target Wisely</strong></h3>\n<p>You’ll be most successful if you focus on one enemy capital at a time. This will allow you to build up a strategy and start catching players who aren’t as ready for you.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Stormwind</strong>: The classic, but often overcrowded. High traffic, but you’re competing with many other gankers.</li>\n<li><strong>Ironforge</strong>: You get fewer but often more vulnerable targets. Great for setting up ambushes.</li>\n<li><strong>Darnassus/Exodar</strong>: Lower traffic, but these capitals have smaller, more manageable choke points. Easier to camp.</li>\n<li><strong>Orgrimmar</strong>: If you’re Horde, consider competing with Alliance players here, since it’s a favorite gank target.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-4-use-warmode-make-a-reputation-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-4-use-warmode-make-a-reputation-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>4. <strong>Use Warmode &amp; Make a Reputation</strong></h3>\n<p>Activate Warmode if you haven’t already. It amplifies the ganking opportunities significantly, especially in capital cities where players often don’t expect ganks.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Create a reputation</strong>: Once you start ganking consistently, you’ll build up a reputation for being a “capital killer.” Your name will spread, and soon you’ll have even more targets coming after you (which, of course, only boosts your kill count).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-5-camp-key-locations-flight-points-bank-ah-etc-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-5-camp-key-locations-flight-points-bank-ah-etc-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>5. <strong>Camp Key Locations (Flight Points, Bank, AH, etc.)</strong></h3>\n<p>Key locations are perfect spots to catch enemies while they’re distracted:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Flight points</strong>: These are often crowded, especially in Stormwind and Orgrimmar. The moment someone lands, they’re a sitting duck.</li>\n<li><strong>Auction House &amp; Bank</strong>: Many players camp these areas to quickly get what they need, making them easy targets.</li>\n<li><strong>Graveyards</strong>: If you’re really daring, camp graveyards after the enemy wipes in a raid or dungeon.</li>\n<li><strong>Innkeepers</strong>: Players often AFK here after a session, making them prime targets.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-6-utilize-world-buffs-toys-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-6-utilize-world-buffs-toys-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>6. <strong>Utilize World Buffs &amp; Toys</strong></h3>\n<p>Utilize every advantage you can get. If you’re looking to maximize efficiency, make sure you’re stacked up on useful world buffs and toys:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Drums of Battle</strong> or <strong>Drums of Speed</strong> – Speed boosts to escape after ganking.</li>\n<li><strong>Flask of the Currents</strong> for enhanced mobility or damage buffs.</li>\n<li><strong>Piccolo of the Flaming Fire</strong> – Make them dance so they can’t escape as easily.</li>\n<li><strong>Toys like the “Springstrider Egg”</strong> or <strong>Disguise Kit</strong> – Keep them guessing with fun disguises or slowing them down with extra CC.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-7-avoid-getting-caught-ganking-counter-strategy-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-7-avoid-getting-caught-ganking-counter-strategy-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>7. <strong>Avoid Getting Caught (Ganking Counter-Strategy)</strong></h3>\n<p>To hit Jackal’s record, you need to minimize your risk of dying to the Alliance who might be looking for revenge:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Learn the flight paths</strong>: Memorize the easiest escape routes if things go south.</li>\n<li><strong>Coordinate with other gankers</strong>: Group up with fellow players who are interested in capital city PvP. This way, if things go south, you can have backup.</li>\n<li><strong>Use “bubble-hearth” or other escape tactics</strong>: This ensures you can vanish if you get overwhelmed.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-8-track-your-progress-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-8-track-your-progress-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>8. <strong>Track Your Progress</strong></h3>\n<p>Since you’re trying to <em>surpass</em> Jackal, tracking your kills is key. Some ideas:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Create a spreadsheet</strong> or use WoW addon trackers like <strong>Advanced Combat Logger</strong> to keep count of your kills.</li>\n<li><strong>Use your own leaderboard</strong> to stay motivated. Aim for milestone goals like 1,000 kills, 5,000 kills, and eventually Jackal’s 10,000.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-9-stay-disciplined-avoid-burnout-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-9-stay-disciplined-avoid-burnout-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>9. <strong>Stay Disciplined &amp; Avoid Burnout</strong></h3>\n<p>Reaching a high kill count isn’t just about going all-out for a few days. The key to surpassing Jackal is consistency and discipline.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Breaks are important</strong>: Avoid long ganking sessions to prevent burnout. Take breaks, focus on other activities, and then return refreshed for another round.</li>\n<li><strong>Always stay alert</strong>: Even after a kill streak, be wary of Alliance groups organizing counter-attacks. Always keep your wits sharp!</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><a name=\"p-27155547-h-10-the-ultimate-goal-break-the-10000-kill-barrier-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-h-10-the-ultimate-goal-break-the-10000-kill-barrier-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a>10. <strong>The Ultimate Goal: Break the 10,000 Kill Barrier</strong></h3>\n<p>Once you’ve surpassed Jackal’s record, <em>you</em> will be the new “Jackal of Azeroth.” Your name will be feared and revered in the cities of the Alliance.</p>\n<p>To truly solidify your place in history, try:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Host a “Gank-a-thon” Event</strong>: Coordinate a massive group of players for a single day of brutal PvP action in the enemy capitals.</li>\n<li><strong>Take screenshots or stream</strong>: Let everyone see you gank your way to glory! You’ll become an internet legend in the process.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h4><a name=\"p-27155547-final-words-12\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-27155547-final-words-12\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"></a><strong>Final Words</strong></h4>\n<p>Surpassing Jackal’s record isn’t just about killing — it’s about becoming a force of nature in the world of World of Warcraft. Stay strategic, patient, and tactical. You’ll get there and more, cementing your place in WoW history!</p>\n<hr>\n<p>This is just impressive. How did it know to include the WARLOCK class among the 3 main stealthers?</p>\n<p>Also, ChatGPT already considered us legends, legendary. A FORCE OF NATURE, which is also true. It’s amazing how A.I. actually understood us better than the community has for many years.</p>",
