        "avatar_template": "https://render.worldofwarcraft.com/classic-us/character/grobbulus/50/66421810-avatar.jpg?alt=/wow/static/images/2d/avatar/2-1.jpg",
        "created_at": "2025-06-29T00:15:10.839Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Too bad it didn’t know that none of the four classes they recommended can bubble hearth, that people getting off FPs are considered Honorless for 20 sec., that streaming runs the risk of being streamsniped(which means the enemy faction can mobilize a far greater force right onto your position), and that camping GYs doesn’t really work in cities. In SW, they start off as a ghost in the Cath Dist, in IF it’s going to be outside the city.</p>\n<p>To get 10,000 would have only taken several months if you no-life it. They’re not all lined up ready to go and enemy player engagement ebbs and flows with the time of day and the stage of a given patch cycle.</p>\n<p>There’s more nuances and secrets that ChatGPT never came close to saying. However, I’m blown away at the overall general advice it gives and how uncannily accurate most of it is.</p>",
